# Installed as /etc/sysusers.d/cathedral-sn39-validator.conf.
#
# The filename must stay validator-specific. The producer host already carries
# /etc/sysusers.d/cathedral-sn39.conf, installed by the evidence producer's own
# deploy tree, and it declares the producer identities (cathedral-evidence,
# cathedral-validator-evidence, and a polaris membership). Shipping this file
# under that generic name overwrites that declaration. systemd-sysusers never
# deletes accounts, so the producer identities would survive on the running
# host and the breakage would stay invisible until someone rebuilt the host
# from its configuration, at which point they would simply be absent.
#
# These are the validator identities only. Producer identities are declared by
# the producer's own deploy tree and are deliberately not restated here.
#
# There is deliberately no cathedral-status identity. The public status
# publisher runs as polaris, which is the account that demonstrably writes
# /var/lib/cathedral-public-evidence/logs on the live host today. A
# cathedral-status account was declared here previously and has never existed
# on the producer host: `id cathedral-status` returns "no such user", while the
# logs directory is polaris:polaris and the publisher that writes it every
# minute runs as polaris. Declaring an account the shipped units then run as,
# on a host where the directory belongs to someone else, produced a unit that
# could not write its own output. Naming the real writer removes the mismatch
# instead of papering over it with a chown that would take the evidence tree
# away from the producer.
g cathedral-validator -
u cathedral-validator - "Cathedral SN39 validator" /var/lib/cathedral-validator /usr/sbin/nologin
#
# polaris is deliberately not made a static member of cathedral-validator-log
# here. It is the producer's account, declared by the producer's deploy tree,
# and this file must not assume it exists on a fresh host. The status publisher
# unit grants itself that group at runtime with SupplementaryGroups=, which
# needs no static membership and no declaration of an account this tree does
# not own.
g cathedral-validator-log -
m cathedral-validator cathedral-validator-log
